Our speakers appear at debates with Völkisch students and with the occasional Freikorps veteran. The nationalist press reports on them with contempt, and printed the same antisemitic slogans the day after as the day before. A handful of young men are won over. Many of our own members, who remember who shot Liebknecht and Luxemburg, are disgusted, and the Left says so loudly.

@reject
subtitle: dev: trust −4, kf_left_dissent −3, kf_right_dissent +3
on-arrival: comintern_trust -= 4; kf_left_dissent -= 3; kf_right_dissent += 3
go-to: root

We keep to the class line: the nationalist youth who march with the Freikorps are the shock troops of the same capital that rules in Paris and in Essen. Moscow notes the disagreement, and the Left, for once, applauds.
